# Real proof search with leanHaT and nanoCoP

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:swi_elixir, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)},
  {:kino, "== 0.19.0"}
])
```

## Introduction

Run two actual theorem provers on quantified formulas, inspect their search
activity, and compare two logics. Sources: [leanHaT](https://leancop.de/leanhat/),
[nanoCoP-i-HT](https://www.leancop.de/ihat/), and the
[TABLEAUX tutorial examples](https://jens-otten.de/tutorial_tableaux19/examples/).

Start with [Getting started](01_basic.livemd) if the wrapper is new to you.
Evaluate top to bottom in a local Livebook runtime on a [supported platform](../README.md#platforms-and-native-bundles).
Setup installs this checkout, its bundled SWI runtime, and Kino; all formulas
and formula generators are visible in the lesson. No solver downloads or
endpoint requests occur when running the examples.

[All chapters](intro.livemd).

